    "albero-vita-title" => "THE TREE OF LIFE",
    "albero-vita-text" => "This tool helps you take stock of the path you have taken so far and your future expectations. Naturally, these are just hypotheses, which you can change even after a short time, perhaps after discussing them with someone you trust.",
    "albero-vita-results" => "Naturally, there is a gap between you and the silhouette you have chosen: life is much richer and more complex than what a drawing can represent. The choice may also depend on factors that can change quickly: your particular mood at the moment, a recent event that happened to you, new people who have entered your horizon, or people you have lost sight of.",

    "albero-title" => "THE TREE OF<br>INFORMAL KNOWLEDGE",
    "albero-text" => "There are skills that arise outside of school and the subjects studied there – for this reason they are defined as 'informal' – which can give rise to promising perspectives and life projects. To make your informal knowledge visible, usable, and communicable, we have used the image of a tree. The fruits hanging from this tree are precisely the informal skills. The roots of this tree are the various aspects that constitute your PERSONAL PROFILE and sink into the soil of your living environments, the affections that nourish you, the friendships you cultivate and draw from, the words and reflections you exchange with those who become part of your world, and the things you see and hear. It is from this humus that your knowledge, both formal and informal, draws nourishment. It is a tree that can grow and develop greatly: other branches and other fruits can continuously be added. Its vitality depends on you and the opportunities provided by your living environment.",
    "albero-results" => "The number of fruits hanging from the branches indicates the richness of your interests and extracurricular skills. Over time, you can update your tree of informal knowledge and, if you wish, make your skills public and available to your community.",

    "ascoltare-title" => "LISTENING",
    "ascoltare-text" => "The primary goal of a listener is to understand what is being said. Understanding is only possible if one can follow along. How can this be achieved? If what is being said is simple and highly interesting, following along is easy and requires no special recommendations. The problem arises when the topics discussed are more complex, require prolonged attention, and do not spark particularly strong interest. This often happens, especially in school, where learning to listen effectively is particularly important because it is one of the main ways to grow both personally and culturally.",
    "ascoltare-results" => "The self-assessment table highlights the aspects where you are well-equipped and those where you should still work to improve your performance.",

    "attenzione-title" => "PAYING ATTENTION",
    "attenzione-text" => "We are all immersed in an enormous amount of stimuli, but only a very small part of these capture our attention and are then remembered. Attention is a filter through which we interact with reality, through which we build our world. There are activities that do not require much effort to pay attention: when we chat with friends, play, or engage in enjoyable activities. In these cases, attention is automatic. When we are exposed to more demanding activities, such as following a lesson explanation, we need to exercise voluntary control over our attention. Since it is normal to get distracted, to maximize the effectiveness of our attention, it is necessary to learn to choose between important things that we absolutely do not want to miss and less significant things.",
    "attenzione-results" => "The map you obtained by completing the questionnaire indicates the six fundamental aspects for managing your attention. The sector where a low score (0/1) appears is the one where you should focus your efforts the most.",

    "attributivo-title" => "ATTRIBUTIVE STYLES<br>AND SELF THEORIES",
    "attributivo-text" => "Sometimes we succeed, sometimes we don't achieve our goals. If things go wrong, we often look for someone to blame: others who are against us, bad luck, our own inability... If things go well, we tend to think we are skilled and that we got what we deserved. The way we assign credit and blame is precisely about the attributive style, which varies among individuals.<br>
	The general idea we have about intelligence greatly influences the attributive style. There are two basic 'theories' about one's intelligence:<span class='break'></span>
	<strong>a)</strong> some believe that intelligence is innate<span class='break'></span>
	<strong>b)</strong> others believe that intelligence develops gradually through knowledge and experiences.<span class='break'></span>
	Obviously, in the first case, one is less inclined to change, whether they think of themselves as brilliant or incapable; in the second case, one is more willing to try different paths.",
    "attributivo-results" => "The graph shows the eight most common attributive styles. By hovering over each style with the mouse, a brief description appears. If, by repeating your evaluation several times over a period, one style prevails over the others, it means that during this time, that is the attributive style that characterizes you the most. You might ask yourself, even discussing it with someone, whether that style is the most favorable for your personal growth.",

    "autostima-title" => "SELF-ESTEEM",
    "autostima-text" => "Self-esteem is like a map that each person consults to understand themselves, especially in moments of crisis or when it is necessary to make a choice. How is it formed? What others say about us, how appreciated we feel, how much confidence we have in our abilities, the tasks we face, and the results we achieve are all ingredients that contribute to the image we form of ourselves. If self-esteem is low, we tend to magnify difficulties and often give up on accepting challenges. If self-esteem is very high, we might have an exaggerated image of our possibilities and could end up disappointed. The best solution would be to have a balanced level of self-esteem. Also because our truest abilities are formed over time, through effective strategies and realistic evaluations of the problems we must face.",
    "autostima-results" => "The data is in percentages: the closer it is to 100%, the higher the self-esteem. More than the global self-esteem, which is given by the average of the scores, it is better to pay attention to the individual areas, because the importance of each can vary from person to person: for example, for one person 'how I feel' may be much more important than 'relationships with others,' or vice versa. Since self-esteem is a construct created by oneself based on one's own history, it is important to know that it is modifiable and controllable, even if the challenge of change is not always easy to accept. The first step is always awareness.",

    "creatività-title" => "CREATIVITY AND<br>SELF-ENTREPRENEURSHIP",
    "creatività-text" => "In any context, the ability to find new solutions, to be proactive, original, autonomous, to take initiative—in a word, to be creative—are admirable qualities, sometimes indispensable. In the workplace, all this translates into 'self-entrepreneurship.' To understand and predict how inclined you are to be self-driven entrepreneurs in the future, you need to ask yourself now how creative you are. This does not necessarily mean being artists or brilliant inventors, but simply possessing, to an adequate degree, the qualities that characterize creative personality and thinking.",
    "creatività-results" => "Each petal of the 'flower' you find in the summary indicates the percentage to which you believe you currently possess the type of thinking or particular quality that generally characterizes a high propensity for creativity and self-entrepreneurship.",

    "imparare-title" => "LEARNING",
    "imparare-text" => "You may have often found yourself struggling to study a text or follow an explanation. Even simply realizing that you do not understand is useful and important. It is the first step, but others must follow, aiming to overcome the difficulties. For this, it is necessary to equip yourself with strategies, especially to tackle new and challenging tasks. Just as a compass is needed to navigate unknown seas, strategies are needed to 'navigate' complex texts.",
    "imparare-results" => "Your self-assessment, which you should verify with the proposed applications, tells you to what extent, for now, you feel equipped, but it also highlights the areas where you can improve your performance.",

    "leggere-title" => "READING",
    "leggere-text" => "People read for various reasons: to study, to seek information, to form opinions, to achieve goals, for the pleasure of imagining and identifying with characters. The way of reading changes depending on the types of text and the reasons for reading. In general, we say that reading is successful when the content of the text is understood: what happens, the connections between different pieces of information, the reasoning proposed, the intentions of the writer, the validity and interest of what is read. As with sports, the more you practice and train, the better you become; the same applies to reading: the more texts of different types you read, the more skilled a reader you become.",
    "leggere-results" => "The self-assessment table presents the different skills activated when reading, and the overall score indicates the probable level you are at now, a level that should be verified with the proposed applications.",

    "motivazione-title" => "MOTIVATION AND<br>AREAS OF INTEREST",
    "motivazione-text" => "Motivation and interest in one activity rather than another, in one subject rather than another, depend on many factors: experiences of success or failure, pleasant or unpleasant situations, the people involved (classmates and teachers) who are likable or unlikable. For these reasons, motivations and interests can also change multiple times over time. However, there are also motivations that remain fairly stable because they depend on our particular aptitudes and characteristics.",
    "motivazione-results" => "The reds and greens on the map are equally important because they can guide you in the choices you will make. The areas of the map largely coincide with higher education and university paths. If you choose an area with reds because friends will be there or to meet parental expectations, there is a risk that sooner or later you will lose the desire to continue. On the contrary, the areas with greens, if you have answered very carefully and thoughtfully, guarantee greater continuity in interest and commitment.",

    "parlare-title" => "SPEAKING",
    "parlare-text" =>  "There are different ways of communicating with the voice. There are easier and more informal forms of communication like confiding and conversing, which, to work, only require willingness and interest in the people you come into contact with. In a conversation, which can take place between a student and someone experienced in some way, an advisor, a teacher, or a trusted adult, the important thing is to have a clear objective for speaking. Discussion is a way of speaking that works when the topic, duration, and goal to be achieved are clear, and you decide what role you want to play: leading, supporting or criticizing, proposing, or simply listening without intervening. In any case, it is advisable to consider that an oral intervention is generally more effective if you know in advance what you want to say and achieve. When intervening, you must make a real contribution; if you feel you cannot, it is better to refrain. You must also consider that what you say can be very important to someone else, bringing them joy or pain, beyond the speaker's intentions. Therefore, you should try to put yourself in the listener's shoes and be careful not to offend or hurt their feelings. To effectively counter another's arguments, you need to grasp the central and weak points of their intervention.",
    "parlare-results" => "The short columns in the self-assessment table indicate the aspects where you feel less equipped, which are worth working on further to improve your performance.",

    "problemi-title" => "SOLVING PROBLEMS",
    "problemi-text" => "There are school problems and life problems, easy problems and difficult problems. Facing and solving problems helps us grow and become more experienced. However, it is not always easy to realize that there is a problem and decide to face it, as we may feel anxious about the fear of failing. Accepting the challenge is the first step, but then we need to find the right strategy to solve it, accepting and overcoming possible failures. When we are convinced of the chosen strategy, we must act by putting it into practice. If the results do not convince us, we must ask ourselves where we went wrong and look for possible remedies. We do not always succeed on our own: asking for help, at the right time and from the right people, can be the winning strategy.",
    "problemi-results" => "You cannot be good at everything: you may be good at solving problems in one area and less skilled, at least for now, in another. After self-assessment, you can test yourself in the two proposed activities. These are logical problems, not simple, but they do not require specific school knowledge. It is not necessary to solve a problem quickly: you can try, leave it for a while, and then come back to it later. If you really cannot manage it on your own, you can always seek collaboration with someone. Many problems are solved only with the help of others.",

    "resilienza-title" => "RESILIENCE",
    "resilienza-text" => "Difficult situations require us to react in some way. From a young age, some of us seem more capable and determined, while others are more insecure and anxious. The ability to react is defined as 'resilience.' Being more resilient makes life easier. It is important to know that resilience can improve significantly over time. This happens if we reflect on what happens to us and seek personal ways to face difficulties.",
    "resilienza-results" => "The position you occupy in the climb to the summit is the average of your evaluations. After reflecting on your individual responses and possibly discussing them with someone, you can retake the questionnaire.",

    "ricordare-title" => "REMEMBERING",
    "ricordare-text" => "Attention, by filtering external and internal stimuli, creates our world. But it is memory that preserves it, longer and more precisely the more stable the traces that are formed. There is a remembering that activates spontaneously and a remembering that requires a choice and intentional effort. Some memories are lost, others last longer, especially if they are used and repeated more often. For this reason, it is advisable to have a method to remember the most important information: ask yourself what use you want to make of the information, choose the most important ones, recall them immediately, and repeat them in a targeted way.",
    "ricordare-results" => "However, we must be aware that we do not all remember in the same way: if you notice that in some aspect of the self-assessment table you are still a bit lacking (column too short), you need to invest more in that particular area.",

    "ruota-title" => "THE WHEEL OF EMOTIONS",
    "ruota-text" => "One can be intelligent in many ways, not just in thinking, but also in experiencing emotions. Emotional intelligence manifests itself at different levels: at the lowest level, there is the ability to feel an emotion, realizing whether one feels good or bad. At a higher level, one is able to recognize and name the emotions they feel and the thoughts linked to them. An even higher level is when one manages to control negative emotions such as anxiety, anger, and sadness. On this basis, the highest level is achieved, which is empathy, the ability to put oneself in the emotional situation that another person is experiencing.",
    "ruota-results" => "There are two indicators that signal progress in becoming more emotionally intelligent: the number of words one possesses to name emotions and how often and easily they are recognized in oneself and others, even in the characters of movies and novels.",

    "scrivere-title" => "WRITING",
    "scrivere-text" => "Writing is a very complex skill that requires intelligence, effort, time, and commitment to learn. However, it should be known that it is an extraordinarily powerful tool, not only for communicating ideas, inventing stories, achieving goals, or making requests, but also and above all for thinking, developing ideas, and discovering.",
    "scrivere-results" => "As you can see on the map, there are many types of writing, for each of which you were asked for a self-assessment. In the questionnaire, however, you expressed your self-assessment for a particular type of writing, which we will define as textual and public, for which you obtained an overall score. To improve your writing ability, you should work on the skills, among the nine listed, in which you still feel lacking.",

    "stili-title" => "COGNITIVE STYLES<br>AND PERSONAL STYLES",
    "stili-text" => "A person's style is also their particular way of learning, tackling problems, and organizing what needs to be done. For example, someone learns more by reading, another by listening. Some of us need to have an overall view of the topic right away to understand, while others understand gradually, following very clear steps. Even when organizing for work, some start with a general intuition, while others plan with many details. Work style also concerns relationships with others: some work better alone, while others are more productive collaborating in a group.<br>
	Often we are partly one way and partly another. Someone, however, has a more 'polarized' style, meaning their way of being is very oriented in one direction. There is no good or bad style. However, understanding how we are is very useful for doing things better and with fewer problems and anxieties.",
    "stili-results" => "There are three possible outcomes:<span class='break'></span>
	<strong>a) Polarized style</strong>, when a certain style, for example 'visual,' is highlighted to the maximum (larger circle), while the opposite style, 'auditory' in our example, is at a minimum (smaller circle or none). In these cases, you might struggle with certain tasks: it is better to train yourself to use the resources you are less inclined to employ.<span class='break'></span>
	<strong>b) Median style</strong>, the most common, when intermediate levels of two opposing styles, such as 'intuitive' and 'systematic,' are highlighted. This means that you generally use the resources suitable for the most varied tasks.<span class='break'></span>
	<strong>c) Flexible style</strong>, when two opposing styles, such as 'collaborative' and 'autonomous,' are highlighted to the maximum. This is a condition similar to the median style but even more favorable because it is more suited to the most varied tasks.",

